version 0.11
symbol diode-2

description Switching diode, 2-pin view: anode, cathode
tags diode
pin_names hide
# The plain diode glyph: the anode triangle points at the cathode bar. This part's datasheet
# numbering runs the other way -- pin 1 is the cathode, pin 2 the anode -- so the pin numbers are
# shown and the reader has to look them up. That is why a rating names its terminals by number and
# not by name (ADR-0026 D4). The names are not drawn: the glyph already says which end is the
# anode, and a name on an artwork body lands on the artwork (the reference project's `d` does the
# same).
# Pin connection points sit on the 0.5 mm placement lattice (ADR-0074); the tails meet the triangle
# and the cathode bar.
field Reference at=[0,2.5] D
field Value at=[0,-2.5] diode-2

pins
  1  [4,0]   180
  2  [-4,0]  0

body
  line  [1.5,-1.5,1.5,1.5]          width=0.25
  poly  [-1.5,1.5,1.5,0,-1.5,-1.5]  width=0.25
